sts, but it may still not be usable: using a folder from a cloud session is not available to everyone yet. Say that plainly, and that they can still do the work in a session that runs on that computer. Do not guess the reason or put it down to their plan or organization. Do not tell the user to run `claude remote-control` to add a folder: for most accounts that command offers nothing to a cloud session, even while it is running, and a folder it does offer is already listed here. Call this before request_computer_folder, when the task needs files, tools or credentials that only exist on the user's computer. Once per session is normally enough: call it again only if the user says they changed the list, or a request was refused because its names did not match. It only reads; it connects nothing. A folder whose `online` is false cannot answer: do not request it. Tell the user that computer is not connected right now (Claude is not running there, or Remote Control is off), ask them to open it, then call this again.", "eager_input_streaming": true, "input_schema": {"properties": {}, "required": [], "type": "object"}, "name": "mcp__claude-code-remote__list_computer_folders"}, "server": "claude-code-remote"}, {"description": "List Claude Code Remote environments for the current user. Returns environment IDs, names, kinds, and states. Use this to pick an environment_id for create_session.", "name": "mcp__claude-code-remote__list_environments", "schema": {"description": "List Claude Code Remote environments for the current user. Returns environment IDs, names, kinds, and states. Use this to pick an environment_id for create_session.", "eager_input_streaming": true, "input_schema": {"properties": {"limit": {"description": "Maximum number of environments to return (default 20, max 100).", "type": "integer"}}, "required": [], "type": "object"}, "name": "mcp__claude-code-remote__list_environments"}, "server": "claude-code-remote"}, {"description": "List transcript events for a Claude Code Remote session (user messages, assistant responses, tool calls, and system events, including model_fallback / model_refusal_fallback notices, which name original_model and fallback_model when the CLI reports them) so you can see what another session is working on. A call with no cursor returns the newest events, in the order they happened; has_more then means older events remain, and before_id set to first_id reads the page before these. A transcript is mostly hook, stream and progress events; to answer a narrow question (what was asked, what the session replied, how a turn ended) pass kinds so the page holds only those events.", "name": "mcp__claude-code-remote__list_events", "schema": {"description": "List transcript events for a Claude Code Remote session (user messages, assistant responses, tool calls, and system events, including model_fallback / model_refusal_fallback notices, which name original_model and fallback_model when the CLI reports them) so you can see what another session is working on. A call with no cursor returns the newest events, in the order they happened; has_more then means older events remain, and before_id set to first_id reads the page before these. A transcript is mostly hook, stream and progress events; to answer a narrow question (what was asked, what the session replied, how a turn ended) pass kinds so the page holds only those events.", "eager_input_streaming": true, "input_schema": {"properties": {"after_id": {"description": "Pagination cursor: return the events just after this event ID. Pass the last_id of the page you hold to move forward, toward newer events.", "type": "string"}, "before_id": {"description": "Pagination cursor: return the events just before this event ID. Pass the first_id of the page you hold to go further back in the transcript.", "type": "string"}, "kinds": {"description": "Return only events of these kinds; omit for every kind. A kind is the key an event carries in data, e.g. [\"user\", \"assistant\